H264 TypeScript API and presentation adapter.

This directory contains the bounded TypeScript adapter and LGPL adaptations.
The caller supplies an explicitly trusted precompiled independent codec module.
No OpenH264 binary or sample media are included in this directory.

The JavaScript display-policy.mjs scheduler adapts FFmpeg's
libavcodec/h264_slice.c (h264_select_output_frame) and libavcodec/h264dec.c
(send_next_delayed_frame/idr) from the repository's pinned upstream submodule.
Copyright (c) 2003 Michael Niedermayer <michaelni@gmx.at>.
Those files' original authors/notices apply; the scheduling adaptation is
LGPL-2.1-or-later. The original source remains in upstream/ffmpeg and the
license text in COPYING.LGPLv2.1 beside this notice.
No FFmpeg implementation is compiled into the OpenH264 Wasm artifact.

Codec binaries, their corresponding sources/build materials and sample media
require their own distribution inventory. This API does not imply CLI support
or complete H264 compatibility.

The independent SPS/PPS parser's VUI field ordering and retained Native
pixel-format lifecycle also follow pinned libavcodec/h264_ps.c,
h2645_vui.c, h2645data.c and h264_slice.c under LGPL-2.1-or-later.
